From a4fa1b02d712fae45f5d06faa8075595244386e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 04:03:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: cut retained memory per effect/computed/atom-dep
 without hurting speed

- ReactiveEffect: pauseCollectChild/resumeCollectChild/dispatch become
  prototype methods (were 3 per-instance arrow closures); constant defaults
  (isRunningAsync/useDepMarker/index/shouldCollectChild) move to the
  prototype; getter/isAsync only become own properties when a getter is
  provided; destroy assigns parent = undefined instead of delete (delete
  pushes the object into dictionary mode)
- Computed: lazily allocate triggerInfos/effectFramesArray/keyToEffectFrames/
  dirtyFromDeps/markedDirtyEffects/savedTriggerInfos/cachedValues; updatedAt
  becomes a plain timestamp with an on-demand atom; recompute/
  recursiveMarkDirty/callGeneratorGetter/manualTrack/pauseAutoTrack/autoTrack/
  resetAutoTrack/collectEffect/destroyEffect become prototype methods with
  lazily bound versions where schedulers need detached callables;
  createGetterContext binds pause/resumeCollectChild explicitly
- atom: primitive atoms share one prototype carrying the raw accessor,
  Symbol.toPrimitive and the IS_ATOM flag; instances keep a single own value
  property (no more per-atom defineProperty)
- Notifier.getOrCreatePrimitiveAtomDep: plain symbol assignment instead of
  defineProperty (kept atoms in fast-properties mode)
- RxList: indexKeyDeps map lazily allocated

Measured with scripts/measure-retained.mjs (node --expose-gc, retained
bytes per object): light binding effect 416B -> 136B, effect+atom+dep
binding 926B -> 621B, computed 2370B -> 627B, empty RxList 5441B -> 1792B.
scripts/measure-speed.mjs shows hot paths equal or faster (effect
create/destroy -18%, RxList splice churn -51%). All 174 tests pass.
